 "text": "Hi, how have you been? He should take the stairway in pairs of stair steps with one hand on wall for balance. Is he able to do that? Then show him in from the front and only stop him at the door. Ask him to remember the number of steps and any landmarks. Then introduce himself. It' worth trying, but it requires a strong and stable chair, and you need to be there to catch him if he falls. Is your landing wide enough? Offer to call him when he arrives, and go inside with him. That's the kindest thing you can do. He' feel valued and needed, and you' have peace of mind too.",
